  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5520",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is linked to G-402 through a series of molecular interactions, with the most direct pathway involving the P2X purinoceptor 1. This receptor is targeted by [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, which in turn has a target of G-402. Another pathway connects doxorubicin to NCI-H46, which is also targeted by the same compound, reinforcing the role of this molecule in mediating the interaction with G-402. Additionally, palmarumycin CP18, which targets G-402, is also linked to doxorubicin via P2X purinoceptor 1. These findings suggest that G-402 is a downstream target of a class of compounds that interact with P2X receptors, potentially through a shared mechanism involving purinergic signaling. The evidence supports a role for these compounds in modulating G-402, though the exact molecular mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
